{"id": "EUVD-2026-71297", "enisaUuid": "9278d1bf-2dc2-3b68-ae1d-47c500112ad7", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ntcp: clamp route advmss to TCP_MIN_MSS\n\ntcp_select_initial_window() assumes that callers never pass an MSS\nsmaller than 1, but route-derived advmss values can violate that\nassumption.\n\nA too-small explicit RTAX_ADVMSS is one way to get there, but it is not\nthe only one. The same divide-by-zero can also be reached through the\n\"default advmss\" path when RTAX_ADVMSS is left at 0 and the effective\nadvmss is later driven down by route MTU and min_adv_mss.\n\nIntroduce a tcp_dst_advmss() helper that clamps route advmss to\nTCP_MIN_MSS before TCP consumes it, and use it in the TCP paths that\nderive advmss from dst metrics. This keeps the effective MSS from\ndropping to zero before tcp_select_initial_window() rounds the receive\nwindow.", "datePublished": "2026-09-04T15:54:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:47:07", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/788fbbf7d61f9742298417c207c91b6db159fbbc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/eaf4af9bd6975c2eff8d48820937c83032d968dc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/cfb44c6028e6f979720315e0772bbd0d4d33ed61", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6b8c20bf61924dfc38fefb145c9f7406d73fae53", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/31cf2349361902769dc323e4dbf4b449795ec288", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/870a9e42ecc6fe1b8c25d87af043cb0d9c178fe1"], "aliases": ["GHSA-m3f3-9j4q-c4f2", "CVE-2026-80847"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "35d79d7e-3c71-34a6-9334-c447095ede42", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2.6.12"}, {"id": "3757dbab-beb6-366c-b397-03c84302b5ea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.3"}, {"id": "4bfa5c8a-708b-3036-ab67-a07e373a6b16", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "p